<title>LITHUANIA: PARLIAMENT PASSES BUTINGE GUARANTEE.</title>
<headline>PARLIAMENT PASSES BUTINGE GUARANTEE.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's parliament on Wednesday approved the government's request to issue a state guarantee to six foreign banks for up to $101.575 million worth of credits to finance the Butinge oil terminal project.</p>
<p>The six banks in the law are the Union Bank of Switzerland (U.S. affiliate) and U.S. EXIM Bank, Kreditanstalt fur Wiederaufbau, Union Bank of Switzerland (Switzerland), Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi, Nordic Investment Bank and Merrill Lynch International.</p>
<p>Parliament passed the measure by a 65-to-27 vote with 14 abstentions, giving the government permission to start negotiations with the banks about loans and conditions.</p>
<p>-- Burton Frierson, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
